 "notes": "Interior of the College of Communication and Media, rebuilt as a scripted area with the main model's sound interior adopted (adopt.json): keep-outs only for what is adopted (the newsroom with its back offices and mezzanine, the south corridor furniture, the atrium group moved square to the shell by T1). Floor 1 slabs reach the walls (the volume rule takes the other sources' ground out of the building). Open questions for Joe: the newsroom office stack (the sign has it about 2.5 m east), the east lounge level (left out: its floor 134.85 and ceiling 138.95 cross floor 1), the lab room (not modelled). College of Communication and Media (CCOM) interior, floors 1 and 2, from Joe's two evacuation floor plans (2026-11-20). Exterior walls, windows and roof: ccom_shell.json. Levels from the main model: floor 1 slabs 137.40 (south) and 137.70 (north), floor 2 slabs 141.85 with soffits at 141.45, floor 2 ceilings 144.86. Wall runs start at 137.30 so they meet both floor 1 levels. The sign plans are diagrams: positions from an evacuation sign, registered to the shell by an affine fit on 9 exterior corners: rms 0.83 m, worst 1.6 m; heights and door widths not on the sign. The room 1000 block (south-west connector, two lifts, a stair) lies inside Morehead Hall's shell in the main model and is not built. The double-height lobby (Joe's photos 1000102886 and 1000102887) is the main model's atrium behind the west doors: its window wall, doors, wood panel wall, stair, glass balustrade, walk-off mat and cube seats exist there (turned 13.7 deg off the shell), so nothing of it is built here; its video wall is missing. Written by a scratch script from pixel positions; edit by hand from here.",
